WEBVTT

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:05.900
A Notice from the Yamayuri Council
When watching
"Maria Watches Over Us ~Printemps~,"
please have the room brightly lit and
sit well away from the television set.

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:22.120
Are you all right?

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:26.120
"All right"? You thought I was crying?

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:27.950
What? You're not?

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:31.850
Your shoulders were trembling the
entire time we were working, so...

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:34.590
That's probably because I was cold.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.930
Then, when it looked like you were sobbing...

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:40.360
I was just sniffling.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:43.470
I thought it would echo too much if
I blew my nose in the gymnasium.

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:45.160
Then this is what you need.

00:00:58.950 --> 00:00:59.750
I guess...

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.180
...it's already the day after tomorrow.

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:03.920
Let's not do this.

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:05.720
It makes me feel sad somehow.

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:07.820
You're right.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:19.610
The maidens, who flock to
Maria-sama's garden,

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:24.240
pass through the tall gates today yet
again with innocent, angelic smiles.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:29.080
Their pure hearts and bodies are
clad in deep-colored uniforms.

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:32.050
So that the pleats of their
skirts are not disturbed...

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:35.510
...and so that their white sailor
collars are not set aflutter,

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:38.850
it is customary here to walk
slowly and with decorum.

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:44.400
The Private Lillian Girls' Academy,
a garden of maidens.

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:57.540
Maria Watches Over Us
Printemps

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:06.550
In the morning mist,
Asamoya no naka

00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:13.460
the white path goes on.
tsuzuku shiroi michi

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:20.930
The birds sing.
Tori no saezuri

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:28.600
We exchange greetings.
Aisatsu kawashinagara

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:36.180
At times, the clouds hang low,
Toki ni kumo ga tarekomete

00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:43.560
and the sun may grow dim.
hizashi kagerou tomo

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:51.690
But I will walk with my chin up,
Sesuji nobashite aruku

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:59.210
for I know,
watashi wa shitteru kara

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:06.050
that above those heavy clouds...
omoi kumo no ue wa

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:14.210
...is the blue sky.
aoi sora

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:28.060
That's right, I still have it easy.

00:03:28.570 --> 00:03:31.270
Shimako-san's big sister is two years older,

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:33.100
so she will be graduating this year.

00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:35.570
Rosa Gigantea...

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:43.980
Eek...

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:45.090
Aww...

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:47.920
R-R-Rosa Chinensis!

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:50.080
W-What kind of joke is this?!

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:51.020
Darn!

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:52.250
"Darn"?

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:56.650
I missed my chance to fully enjoy the
experience of cuddling Yumi-chan.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:04:00.440
And Sei said you make
sounds like a baby dinosaur,

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:01.990
so I was looking forward to it.

00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:03.670
I see...

00:04:04.270 --> 00:04:06.710
I just wanted to try it once.

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:10.180
The unique experience of being a
pseudo-serial hugger with you.

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:12.310
I can't do it anymore once I graduate, right?

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:16.010
Since it's not as if I'm going
to the affiliate college.

00:04:16.550 --> 00:04:18.080
Please come visit us.

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:20.120
Yes...

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:25.730
Yumi-chan, keep me company for a bit.

00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:26.380
What?

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:29.260
Uh, um, Rosa Chinensis...

00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:30.800
Just come along.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:33.790
Humor your old granny for once.

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:38.800
Okay, don't be shy. Drink up.

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:44.040
What? Well, but it's hot,
so I can't gulp it down that quickly.

00:04:44.210 --> 00:04:45.110
Really?

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:49.310
Wh-Wh-Wh-What are you doing?!

00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:52.190
What am I doing? Isn't it obvious?

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:54.310
W-W-Why?

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:56.790
You just said it's too hot to drink.

00:04:57.260 --> 00:04:59.160
Well, I did say that, but...

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:06.700
This doesn't taste that good, does it?

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:08.760
T-That's not true!

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:14.230
Thanks for the treat!

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:16.280
Rosa Chinensis...

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:20.450
Was this something you wanted to try once, too?

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:22.050
That's right.

00:05:23.150 --> 00:05:25.020
You're very perceptive, Yumi-chan.

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:25.910
Ahh...

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:27.610
And also interesting.

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:28.980
Um...

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:31.560
That's why I think very highly of you.

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:36.130
So, um, is that to say,
that's why I was singled out...

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:40.120
...as someone who had experience
with hot strawberry milk au lait?

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:43.570
No, as Sachiko's guardian.

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:45.130
Pardon?

00:05:45.970 --> 00:05:50.170
Yumi-chan, please take care of Sachiko for me.

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:53.110
I will...

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:59.110
She's not very endearing, but even so,
she's my dearly beloved little sister.

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:04.460
I am not perceptive by any means.

00:06:06.230 --> 00:06:10.330
Rosa Chinensis invited me along
to convey her "will" to me.

00:06:10.330 --> 00:06:13.790
But it was only in that moment
that I finally realized this.

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:16.060
What were you doing?

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:19.000
I am so sorry for being late.

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:21.180
I believe I told you to come early today,

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:24.300
because we would be cleaning
out the first floor storeroom.

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:25.970
Yes, I am sorry!

00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:28.380
I am asking what you were doing.

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:33.650
Um... I was invited along by
Rosa Chinensis... to the milk bar...

00:06:33.650 --> 00:06:34.640
By my Onee-sama?

00:06:35.390 --> 00:06:37.020
I see, I understand.

00:06:38.930 --> 00:06:40.550
Then, let us begin.

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:43.460
Yumi, you can join us after
you have cleaned up here.

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:44.960
All right.

00:06:46.370 --> 00:06:47.430
Don't let it bother you.

00:06:47.570 --> 00:06:51.230
Sachiko is only irritated because
she was worried about you.

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:53.340
Rei, what are you muttering about?!

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:54.180
Nothing!

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:54.800
See you later.

00:06:55.110 --> 00:06:57.710
Ooh, so scary! Sachiko's throwing a fit.

00:06:57.710 --> 00:06:58.800
Excuse me?!

00:06:58.880 --> 00:06:59.640
There, that's it.

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:01.980
Storing up your anger isn't good for you.

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:07.350
I feel like I can understand why
she conveyed her "will" to you.

00:07:07.490 --> 00:07:08.350
Understand?

00:07:08.620 --> 00:07:09.820
You see,

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:11.730
when people move on to
a different environment...

00:07:11.730 --> 00:07:13.830
...from a place they've long been familiar with,

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:17.290
they tend to be keenly aware
of the things they've left undone.

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:18.720
And thus, a "will"...

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:21.770
Rosa Foetida asked to see me, too.

00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:22.430
What?

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:25.760
Our relationship comes down to a
triangle with Rei-chan in the middle.

00:07:26.410 --> 00:07:28.640
So naturally, there are a lot of
things we want to say to each other.

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:29.800
Things you want to say?

00:07:30.140 --> 00:07:31.870
About each other's strengths.

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:35.520
We go over every little thing, even
things like our attitude towards life.

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:38.390
Well, it's not the sort of
argument that can be settled.

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:40.450
It's just for show, if you will.

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:42.490
For show...

00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:47.060
Everyone's doing all sorts of things.

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:48.830
Their methods might differ,

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:51.890
but they're all reluctant to say
good-bye in their own way.

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:56.500
I see... And my Onee-sama knew that...

00:07:59.910 --> 00:08:00.840
Here, look.

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:03.410
We found all these personal
belongings of Rosa Gigantea's.

00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:06.080
A textbook, a sports towel...

00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:10.010
Oh, this is the lunch box that
she made a big fuss about losing.

00:08:10.450 --> 00:08:12.540
It had fallen between some cardboard boxes.

00:08:12.690 --> 00:08:16.920
But my Onee-sama insisted
that it had to be upstairs,

00:08:16.920 --> 00:08:18.290
so we all looked for it.

00:08:18.730 --> 00:08:20.800
She must have had lunch upstairs,

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:23.200
then dropped by this room on her way home.

00:08:23.700 --> 00:08:25.690
But she had convinced herself otherwise.

00:08:26.070 --> 00:08:27.730
No wonder we couldn't find it.

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:30.070
Oh, Rosa Gigantea...

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:32.800
Cinderella Props

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:36.140
Hey, are these the props we used for Cinderella?

00:08:36.380 --> 00:08:39.010
Oh, Rosa Foetida's handkerchief.

00:08:39.310 --> 00:08:42.750
This is my Onee-sama's mechanical pencil.

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:45.090
They have no names on them.

00:08:45.090 --> 00:08:47.080
I am amazed you know who they belong to.

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:48.790
Of course, we can tell.

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:53.090
Because we are their little sisters.

00:08:57.830 --> 00:09:00.270
I shall return it to her tomorrow.

00:09:06.370 --> 00:09:08.770
My Onee-sama's "will"?

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:12.310
Right, like about something
she wants you to do...

00:09:12.310 --> 00:09:15.450
...or about how she wants you
to guard the school traditions...

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:16.940
Has she said anything like that?

00:09:17.390 --> 00:09:18.910
A "will"...

00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:21.280
She is not the sort to speak of such things.

00:09:22.420 --> 00:09:24.910
At the very least, she wouldn't say it to me.

00:09:25.030 --> 00:09:26.080
I see.

00:09:26.390 --> 00:09:27.590
I guess you're right.

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:31.090
But she might have something to say to you.

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:32.230
Me?

00:09:32.330 --> 00:09:36.570
Yes, because my dear sister
has great affection for you.

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:39.300
I'm sorry.

00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:40.540
Why?

00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:44.180
I think I may have been leaning
on Rosa Gigantea for support...

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:46.580
...without considering how
it might make you feel.

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:47.810
Oh, please.

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:50.580
Such a thought has never
once crossed my mind.

00:09:50.750 --> 00:09:54.920
You know, if anything,
I'm actually grateful to you.

00:09:55.060 --> 00:09:55.680
What?

00:09:56.760 --> 00:09:59.520
I'm not good at leaning on others for support...

00:09:59.930 --> 00:10:03.020
...and that was never a part of our
relationship as sisters to begin with.

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:05.060
And because we're two years apart,

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:06.800
even if she wanted to dote on someone,

00:10:06.800 --> 00:10:08.840
in Rosa Gigantea's case,

00:10:08.840 --> 00:10:10.900
her little sister doesn't even have a little sister.

00:10:11.270 --> 00:10:13.040
You mean, like a "granddaughter"?

00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:16.440
Granddaughter? Oh yes, something like that.

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:18.980
Since your little sister...

00:10:18.980 --> 00:10:22.210
...will be enrolling as Rosa Gigantea is leaving.

00:10:22.780 --> 00:10:25.010
A little sister...

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:27.250
I can't even imagine having one, though...

00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:31.460
But maybe Rosa Gigantea
also had similar thoughts...

00:10:31.460 --> 00:10:33.520
...when she became soeurs with you.

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:35.380
Yes...

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:39.270
Whether I can find an underclassman
whom I can get along with...

00:10:39.270 --> 00:10:40.890
...is one issue,

00:10:41.370 --> 00:10:43.300
but if I come to have a little sister,

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:45.370
as a first-year student,

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:48.040
she will have to become the
Rosa Gigantea en bouton, right?

00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:50.640
But that's what you did, too.

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:53.070
Yes, of course,

00:10:53.510 --> 00:10:58.610
but I have this vague feeling that
perhaps I must not have a little sister.

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:03.780
Shimako-san!

00:11:03.860 --> 00:11:04.930
What? What is it?

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:06.860
Shimako-san, please don't go anywhere!

00:11:06.860 --> 00:11:07.690
Yumi-san?

00:11:07.860 --> 00:11:09.760
Please don't go anywhere, and wait for me...

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:11.820
...until I become a third-year student!

00:11:12.170 --> 00:11:14.700
We're going to carry on the
Yamayuri Council together!

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:17.190
I don't want to do it without you!

00:11:20.110 --> 00:11:21.070
Um...

00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:22.400
Fukuzawa-san.

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:28.080
I'm sorry to put a damper
on your beautiful friendship,

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:31.070
but please take your seat.
I'd like to begin homeroom.

00:11:32.020 --> 00:11:33.110
Pardon me!

00:11:41.030 --> 00:11:45.930
"Th-ank you"...

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:57.470
Now that I think about it,

00:11:57.580 --> 00:12:00.920
if Rosa Gigantea were to have concerns...

00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:03.120
...and they had to do with Shimako-san,

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:04.880
there's no way she would
say that to Shimako-san.

00:12:19.370 --> 00:12:22.340
We could always find our dear
third-year sisters in these classrooms...

00:12:22.940 --> 00:12:25.500
But even that will come to an end tomorrow...

00:12:33.510 --> 00:12:35.780
Rosa Gigantea's classroom...

00:12:47.190 --> 00:12:48.530
Did you forget something?

00:12:49.400 --> 00:12:50.730
Oh, Yumi-chan.

00:12:53.570 --> 00:12:55.030
Sorry, but would you close that?

00:13:00.470 --> 00:13:03.410
I wanted to say good-bye to the classroom,

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:05.680
so I killed time in the library...

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:09.240
...and came back when I figured
that everyone would have left.

00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:10.610
Go ahead and laugh.

00:13:13.190 --> 00:13:14.720
When I thought about how...

00:13:14.720 --> 00:13:18.560
...I have to leave this place
behind as of tomorrow,

00:13:18.560 --> 00:13:20.490
I got a bit sentimental.

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:23.360
Because you will be leaving Lillian?

00:13:29.340 --> 00:13:30.890
A lot has happened, after all.

00:13:31.670 --> 00:13:32.570
A lot?

00:13:33.810 --> 00:13:36.500
Happy experiences, painful experiences...

00:13:36.910 --> 00:13:41.080
There are things I regret,
but also great memories...

00:13:42.620 --> 00:13:44.910
These three years in high school...

00:13:44.990 --> 00:13:49.320
...were the most enriching years
of my life thus far, I think.

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:55.100
Rosa Gigantea, I...

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:56.890
W-What is it, Yumi-chan?

00:13:57.300 --> 00:13:59.790
Is there anything that I can do?!

00:14:00.200 --> 00:14:01.100
That you can do?

00:14:01.270 --> 00:14:06.640
Any requests or favors or promises or
something you want to entrust to me?

00:14:06.770 --> 00:14:08.000
What's this about?

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:10.600
Anything is fine.

00:14:10.710 --> 00:14:12.350
Something to do with Shimako-san, for example.

00:14:12.350 --> 00:14:14.910
Or to do with Lunch... I mean, Goronta.

00:14:15.050 --> 00:14:16.910
There must be something! At least one thing!

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:18.150
There isn't.

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:20.820
Like I said, there isn't.

00:14:21.090 --> 00:14:23.520
There isn't anything I want to ask of you.

00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:26.760
And Goronta's all grown up now,

00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:29.750
so he'll be fine,
even without humans to feed him.

00:14:30.030 --> 00:14:31.570
If he can't survive on his own,

00:14:31.570 --> 00:14:33.230
there's no point in him being a stray anyway.

00:14:33.870 --> 00:14:36.430
Besides, I don't need to ask.

00:14:36.670 --> 00:14:39.940
You wouldn't be able to ignore it
if Shimako got in trouble, right?

00:14:40.010 --> 00:14:42.210
Even if you had to do something scandalous,

00:14:42.210 --> 00:14:45.700
you would surely throw yourself into
the maelstrom to save Shimako.

00:14:46.550 --> 00:14:49.740
There's a genuine friendship between you two.

00:14:49.880 --> 00:14:51.720
There's no need for me to will anything.

00:14:52.250 --> 00:14:55.160
Besides, if you were the sort of person...

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:57.730
...who wouldn't help others
unless you were asked to,

00:14:57.730 --> 00:15:01.250
again, I wouldn't ask you
to be there for Shimako.

00:15:01.530 --> 00:15:05.230
But I want to do something
for you, Rosa Gigantea...

00:15:05.330 --> 00:15:06.730
A so-called parting gift?

00:15:07.200 --> 00:15:08.330
Well...

00:15:08.700 --> 00:15:11.760
Then maybe I'll ask you for a kiss on the mouth.

00:15:11.910 --> 00:15:12.430
What?

00:15:12.540 --> 00:15:14.100
Oh? You gonna run away?

00:15:14.210 --> 00:15:16.110
You said it could be anything.

00:15:17.140 --> 00:15:19.240
Here, be good and close your eyes.

00:15:24.420 --> 00:15:25.180
Cut!

00:15:25.950 --> 00:15:27.180
G-Good-bye!

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:35.650
I can't graduate, because I'll
forever regret not kissing you.

00:15:39.270 --> 00:15:39.960
What's wrong?

00:15:46.440 --> 00:15:48.770
If you don't hurry on home,
I'll come after you again.

00:15:51.480 --> 00:15:52.710
What are you thinking?

00:16:16.840 --> 00:16:20.710
I didn't think it needed to be said in
so many words, so I'd kept quiet,

00:16:20.710 --> 00:16:25.810
but from the bottom of my heart,
I feel glad that I got to know you.

00:16:25.950 --> 00:16:26.410
What?

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:33.080
I never got along very well
with normal girls my age.

00:16:33.590 --> 00:16:38.750
Seeing you, for the first time in
my life, I envied normal girls.

00:16:40.760 --> 00:16:45.160
In my third year, I was able
to change in a good way.

00:16:46.070 --> 00:16:48.090
Life has become quite a bit more bearable.

00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:52.840
There are a lot of reasons as
for why I was able to change,

00:16:52.840 --> 00:16:55.930
but you should know,
you were a big part of it.

00:16:56.680 --> 00:16:59.480
So, what you've done for me...

00:16:59.480 --> 00:17:01.410
...isn't just that kiss.

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:03.740
What did I ever do?

00:17:04.050 --> 00:17:06.350
Open your ears wide and listen carefully.

00:17:06.990 --> 00:17:09.960
You made me a college student, didn't you?

00:17:10.060 --> 00:17:10.820
No way.

00:17:10.990 --> 00:17:11.860
It's true.

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:17.090
Seeing you, I decided to
try being a student again.

00:17:17.500 --> 00:17:19.230
Seeing me?

00:17:19.300 --> 00:17:22.270
So you see, Yumi-chan, you should
have confidence in yourself.

00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:27.030
Since you got someone as cool
as me aspiring to be like you.

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:29.200
That is all. Bow.

00:17:32.350 --> 00:17:34.440
I love you, Yumi-chan.

00:17:34.850 --> 00:17:38.280
I was truly happy when I got
to goof around with you.

00:17:38.420 --> 00:17:42.320
There were many times when
I wished I could be you.

00:17:48.430 --> 00:17:50.560
You tell everyone that you love them, don't you?

00:17:51.100 --> 00:17:51.560
Yup.

00:17:52.370 --> 00:17:53.230
Honestly...

00:17:53.900 --> 00:17:55.460
Thanks for the smooch.

00:17:56.200 --> 00:17:59.070
Think nothing of it. It was just a parting gift.

00:17:59.370 --> 00:18:00.600
Just a parting gift, huh?

00:18:01.240 --> 00:18:05.140
By the way, do you know
which college I'm going to?

00:18:05.410 --> 00:18:06.000
Huh?

00:18:06.610 --> 00:18:07.980
No, it's fine.

00:18:08.420 --> 00:18:11.090
I was thinking you might
have been running around,

00:18:11.090 --> 00:18:13.140
trying not to hear the name of the college.

00:18:13.320 --> 00:18:14.820
Because it would be like...

00:18:14.820 --> 00:18:17.150
...the college was stealing away
your beloved Rosa Gigantea.

00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:19.150
You think too highly of yourself.

00:18:27.530 --> 00:18:29.000
She was right on the mark.

00:18:29.140 --> 00:18:31.660
Rosa Gigantea is so perceptive.

00:18:32.370 --> 00:18:35.540
I knew she would be going
somewhere beyond my reach...

00:18:35.540 --> 00:18:37.480
...and I didn't want to make it seem real.

00:18:37.680 --> 00:18:39.480
I was running away from that.

00:19:08.980 --> 00:19:12.140
I was tricked! I was tricked! I was tricked!

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:16.040
Rosa Gigantea!

00:19:18.850 --> 00:19:19.980
Yumi-chan.

00:19:20.150 --> 00:19:22.650
That's quite a scowl you got there. What's up?

00:19:23.020 --> 00:19:26.860
Good day. Congratulations on graduating today.

00:19:26.930 --> 00:19:28.190
Right, thank you.

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:30.700
W-Where are we going?

00:19:30.700 --> 00:19:32.130
Somewhere where we can be alone!

00:19:32.300 --> 00:19:34.390
Sounds good. Wanna pick up
where we left off yesterday?

00:19:34.740 --> 00:19:36.600
That is what I would like a word with you about.

00:19:39.910 --> 00:19:41.100
So, what is it?

00:19:41.610 --> 00:19:42.730
Is it true?

00:19:43.080 --> 00:19:44.200
Is what true?

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:45.940
About college.

00:19:46.050 --> 00:19:47.100
About college?

00:19:47.180 --> 00:19:48.650
There you go again, playing dumb!

00:19:48.650 --> 00:19:50.180
Oh, did you find out?

00:19:50.180 --> 00:19:51.550
That was faster than I expected.

00:19:51.550 --> 00:19:53.680
I asked Shimako-san about it this morning!

00:19:54.150 --> 00:19:55.680
What? My Onee-sama?

00:19:56.190 --> 00:19:58.490
She's going to Lillian Ladies' College.

00:19:58.660 --> 00:19:59.320
What?!

00:19:59.660 --> 00:20:03.230
But she didn't turn in the priority
acceptance application in time,

00:20:03.230 --> 00:20:05.060
so she said she went on to take entrance exams!

00:20:05.130 --> 00:20:07.970
Yes, and she took the exams for Lillian,

00:20:07.970 --> 00:20:09.960
along with all the non-Lillian applicants.

00:20:12.110 --> 00:20:13.970
WHAT?!

00:20:14.780 --> 00:20:16.880
I was such a complete fool!

00:20:16.880 --> 00:20:19.280
I was so embarrassed, my face was ablaze!

00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:22.010
What? I would have loved to see that!

00:20:22.220 --> 00:20:24.590
Keep teasing and I will punch your lights out.

00:20:24.590 --> 00:20:26.210
Whoa... Is this payback?

00:20:27.890 --> 00:20:29.550
Don't be so snarly.

00:20:29.990 --> 00:20:33.550
It was definitely my fault for
not informing you properly.

00:20:33.690 --> 00:20:37.460
But who would normally think
that you wouldn't know?

00:20:37.660 --> 00:20:39.290
Weren't you intentionally keeping it from me?

00:20:39.400 --> 00:20:41.670
What for? For the smooch?

00:20:41.670 --> 00:20:42.790
Don't talk about that!

00:20:44.810 --> 00:20:45.970
What does it really matter?

00:20:46.410 --> 00:20:47.960
It's true that I'm graduating.

00:20:48.480 --> 00:20:50.200
It's also true that I'm going to college.

00:20:50.340 --> 00:20:52.040
So I took my parting gift.

00:20:52.610 --> 00:20:54.080
Where's the problem in that?

00:20:54.480 --> 00:20:56.310
But you're going to Lillian Ladies'.

00:20:56.650 --> 00:20:57.210
Yeah.

00:21:02.990 --> 00:21:05.980
I'm not going to college for the sake of studying.

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:09.790
It's so I can get acclimated to
the idea of "school," if you will.

00:21:10.130 --> 00:21:12.720
I'm going so I can come
to terms with it emotionally.

00:21:13.170 --> 00:21:16.290
So, the place needed to be Lillian.

00:21:16.500 --> 00:21:20.740
Besides, I'm not going to visit the
high school once I graduate.

00:21:22.410 --> 00:21:23.570
You aren't?

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:27.870
I'll be the same as Yoko and Eriko,
who are going to separate colleges.

00:21:28.980 --> 00:21:31.640
Is that her way of telling me
not to depend on her?

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:32.990
And yet, even so,

00:21:32.990 --> 00:21:35.990
the sense of reassurance that she'll
be on the same school grounds...

00:21:35.990 --> 00:21:37.350
...makes me a little happy.

00:21:38.160 --> 00:21:39.560
It makes me really happy.

00:21:45.770 --> 00:21:48.360
Too bad. Time's almost up.

00:21:49.340 --> 00:21:50.100
Yes.

00:21:53.040 --> 00:21:54.030
Well, see you later.

00:21:54.210 --> 00:21:55.640
Yes, see you again later.

00:22:09.160 --> 00:22:12.960
Rosa Gigantea, go ahead
and graduate. I'll be fine.

00:23:26.770 --> 00:23:29.760
Onee-sama, I guess the Lady
Roses are finally graduating.

00:23:29.840 --> 00:23:30.700
Yes, meow.

00:23:30.800 --> 00:23:32.200
We'll miss them dearly, won't we?

00:23:32.340 --> 00:23:33.400
Indeed, meow.

00:23:33.510 --> 00:23:36.270
Are you taking this opportunity
to change your character?

00:23:36.380 --> 00:23:38.400
I want you to call me Sachiko-meow
from now on, meow.

00:23:38.480 --> 00:23:41.110
That sounds great! Shall we all wear cat ears?

00:23:41.250 --> 00:23:43.440
So we'll be red, white, and yellow cats.

00:23:43.580 --> 00:23:44.850
It'll be the Yamaneko Council, meow.

00:23:44.950 --> 00:23:46.940
Then we shall say it's the Acorn Mansion.

00:23:47.020 --> 00:23:49.050
This is great, it's like Kenji Miyazawa, meow.

00:23:49.120 --> 00:23:49.760
Next time on "Maria Watches Over Us," meow,

00:23:49.760 --> 00:23:51.490
Next time on "Maria Watches Over Us," meow,
Next Time "The Years That Flew By"

00:23:51.490 --> 00:23:52.730
"The Years That Flew By".
Next Time "The Years That Flew By"

00:23:52.730 --> 00:23:53.730
We hope you watch, meow.
Next Time "The Years That Flew By"

00:23:53.730 --> 00:23:54.160
Meow.
Next Time "The Years That Flew By"

00:23:54.160 --> 00:23:54.290
Meow.
Meow.
Next Time "The Years That Flew By"

00:23:54.290 --> 00:23:54.930
Meow.
